;; Written by Claude, 2026-10-14, for Phase 17 (design section 20,
;; proposal 8, approved by the user); reviewed by the user, 2026-10-14. It
;; replaces the file the user reviewed on 2026-10-08. Why this is right:
;; - Each of the 4 FOR loops ends before a step that would pass its
;;   final value (proposal 8), as on LLVM: after the body, SUBx3 at the
;;   variable's width computes the distance left (the final value less
;;   the variable counting up, the variable less the final value
;;   counting down), CMPx compares it with the step's size, and BGEQU
;;   goes on to the step, else JMP L^ leaves the loop. Each adds one
;;   label, so the labels after each are numbered one more.
;; The rest is as the user reviewed it on 2026-10-08:
;; - COPY(x, v) with x or v longer than 65535 characters, LOCC's and
;;   MOVC5's most, is done in pieces (decided with the user 2026-10-08):
;;   m, the most characters it may copy, is LEN(v) - 1, or LEN(x) if
;;   less. LOCC #0 searches at most 65535 bytes at a time from R1, R2 the
;;   bytes left; it leaves R1 at the 0X when it finds one (Z clear) or past
;;   the piece (MACRO 9-130), so R1 less x's address is n, the characters
;;   to copy, pushed on the stack. MOVC3 then moves at most 65535 of them
;;   at a time, from where the last left R1 and R3 (MACRO 9-132), the count
;;   left on the stack as MOVC3 overwrites R0-R5; CLRB (R3) puts the 0X
;;   after the last, and the rest of v is left as it was.
;; - The runs find the 0X in the second piece (69000), the first (10) and
;;   not at all (70000, all of x), and copy into mid, which takes 65999,
;;   and small, 9, and through CopyTo's VAR parameter, @4(AP). EXAMINE
;;   shows an offset above 65535 as an address, not a symbol.
;; - A string constant still takes one MOVC5, as in vax-copy.
;; - Step 8 (decided 2026-10-08) adds the module's key, POC_K1_ and its
;;   .sym's key, a global symbol its importers declare .EXTERNAL, and, as
;;   it is the program's main module, the program's start,
;;   VAXCOPYLONG_MAIN, which calls the initializer, returns SS$_NORMAL
;;   and is named by .END.
